Horizon OC clock-manager IPC client
===================================

These files are vendored unmodified from the Horizon OC project (by way of
Status-Monitor-Overlay, which ships the same client). They are used to read the
CPU / GPU / RAM die temperatures that Horizon OC's sysmodule exposes over IPC.
Those sensors live in the Tegra SOC_THERM block behind MMIO that a homebrew
application cannot map, so asking Horizon OC is the only way to reach them
without writing a SOC_THERM driver.

They are licensed under the GNU GPL v2, alongside the sys-clk Beer-Ware notice,
and those notices are preserved verbatim in each file. NX-FanControl as a whole
is distributed under the GNU GPL v2 (see ../../../LICENSE), so these files are
under the same terms as the project that uses them.

